// title: Which devices carry a registry tag, and how it compares with their portal and dynamic tags
// date: 2026-10-13
// product: Defender for Endpoint
// tables: DeviceInfo
// purpose: Lists, for every device seen in seven days, the tag written through the registry next to the tags set in the portal or API and by dynamic rules. A device whose registry tag differs from its manual tags is one where a registry-reading script gives the wrong answer; MachineGroup shows which RBAC devic
// source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-xdr/advanced-hunting-deviceinfo-table
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l)
// Microsoft SOC Brief 13 Oct 2026 - device tags: registry tag against portal and dynamic tags
// Defender XDR advanced hunting. Columns as on the DeviceInfo schema page cited beside this query. Not run against a tenant in this pass.
DeviceInfo
| where Timestamp > ago(7d)
| summarize arg_max(Timestamp, DeviceName, MachineGroup, RegistryDeviceTag, DeviceManualTags, DeviceDynamicTags) by DeviceId
| where isnotempty(RegistryDeviceTag) or isnotempty(DeviceManualTags) or isnotempty(DeviceDynamicTags)
| project DeviceName, MachineGroup, RegistryDeviceTag, DeviceManualTags, DeviceDynamicTags
| order by MachineGroup asc, DeviceName asc
